+// g-lab-bit fork (incremental_objects.patch): FPDF_VerifyIncrementalSave().
+//
+// Compares objects of the in-memory document ("memory") with the same object
+// numbers in an independently parsed saved file ("saved"). The memory side
+// is only read: references there are never resolved through the memory
+// document's parser (that would load objects into its map), only through
+// GetIndirectObject(), which does not parse.
+//
+// PDFium changes objects after load without a user edit. Each such change
+// is handled here explicitly:
+//  M1 Stream /Length is replaced by a direct number when a stream is loaded
+//     (CPDF_Stream::SetLengthInDict), on both sides: /Length is skipped and
+//     the data is compared instead.
+//  M2 Encrypted strings/streams are decrypted on load
+//     (CPDF_CryptoHandler::DecryptObjectTree), on both sides: decrypted
+//     values are compared.
+//  M3 The writer Flate-encodes unfiltered streams and drops their
+//     /DecodeParms (CPDF_FlateEncoder): memory without /Filter vs. saved
+//     /Filter /FlateDecode compares memory data with decoded saved data.
+//  M4 A page object without /Type gets /Type /Page when the page is loaded
+//     (CPDF_Page's constructor), and page tree nodes visited by
+//     CountPages()/TraversePDFPages() get /Type /Pages or /Page
+//     (GetNodeType()). Accepted only for dictionaries of the page tree
+//     (reachable from /Root /Pages via /Kids), only for exactly that value,
+//     and only against a saved /Type that is missing or not Page/Pages.
+//  M5 An invalid page tree /Count is recomputed (CountPages()): accepted
+//     only on page tree nodes, against a saved /Count PDFium would replace
+//     (not in 1..kPageMaxNum-1).
+//  M6 Direct page dictionaries in /Kids become indirect objects when a page
+//     is loaded (TraversePDFPages): NOT tolerated. FPDF_SaveIncrementalObjects
+//     refuses such a document unless the /Pages node is listed, so a
+//     mismatch here is real.
+//  M7 With an interactive form, CPDF_InteractiveForm::LoadField /
+//     AddTerminalField (also via FixPageFields when a form page view is
+//     created) (a) replaces an indirect /T with a direct copy of the string
+//     (an empty string if the target is not a string), and (b) copies /FT
+//     and /Ff from a widget without /T to its /Parent when the parent has
+//     no /FT. Accepted only for dictionaries of the field tree (reachable
+//     from /Root /AcroForm /Fields via /Kids) and only for exactly the value
+//     LoadField would produce: for (b) the saved parent must lack /FT, and
+//     the value is the one of the first qualifying kid in /Kids order (if
+//     the pages list the widgets in another order, the result may be a
+//     conservative FALSE).
+//  Rendering writes nothing to the document map: fork_p8 generates
+//  appearances (incl. the /AS fix) into private CPDF_IndirectObjectHolders
+//  and creates popups as direct dictionaries outside /Annots, and inline
+//  image dictionaries belong to the content parser.
+//  Anything else that differs (e.g. /AcroForm /DR fonts added while editing
+//  a text field) is an edit and must have been saved.
+constexpr int kMaxCompareDepth = 64;
+constexpr int kMaxTreeDepth = 64;
+
+template <typename Fn>
+void ForEachRef(RetainPtr<const CPDF_Object> obj, Fn fn) {
+  CPDF_ObjectWalker walker(std::move(obj));
+  while (RetainPtr<const CPDF_Object> sub = walker.GetNext()) {
+    if (const CPDF_Reference* ref = sub->AsReference()) {
+      fn(ref->GetRefObjNum());
+    }
+  }
+}
